    <name>🌡️ LIVE WATER TEMPERATURE</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>GREAT LAKES SURFACE WATER TEMPERATURE</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-21 06:50 UTC<br/><b>Source updated:</b> Mon, 21 Sep 2026 06:50:54 GMT<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-21 21:58 UTC<br/><b>Status:</b> CURRENT DAILY (satellite composite)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/water_temperature/legend.png?v=2026-09-21_2158_UTC" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Surface water temperature (°F): cold <b>52°F</b> (deep blue) → <b>63°F</b> → warm <b>74°F</b> (red). Lakewide mean this run: <b>64.3°F</b>.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/GLERL CoastWatch GLSEA (Great Lakes Surface Environmental Analysis)<br/><a href="https://apps.glerl.noaa.gov/coastwatch/webdata/glsea/cur/glsea_cur.asc">https://apps.glerl.noaa.gov/coastwatch/webdata/glsea/cur/glsea_cur.asc</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of wave and ice layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
